Two gaps that need a merge-time check, both documented in the action's
description. Neither is closable at pull_request_target time:

- merge queues. A pull_request_target workflow never runs on `merge_group`, so a
  repo that enables a merge queue would have entries wait for a check that never
  arrives, time out (60 min default) and be dequeued -- every PR in that repo
  unmergeable. Extend the gate BEFORE any repo turns a queue on: parse the PR
  number out of refs/heads/gh-readonly-queue/<base>/pr-<N>-<sha> and read the
  body with `body-source: api`, since there is no pull_request payload there.

- a description edited with GITHUB_TOKEN does not start a new workflow run, so
  an automation calling `gh pr edit --body ''` leaves the earlier green result
  standing. Wants either the merge_group leg above or a post-merge audit on
  `push: main` that re-reads the merged PR's body and opens an issue on
  mismatch.


