- vars.HPC_CI_REMOTE_WORK_DIR = '$SCRATCH/downstream-ci' is the ONE setting the
  HPC path needs, and it is being set now. Single-quote it: the spec is expanded
  on the cluster, in a login shell, not on the runner. It has no fallback by
  design (build-on-hpc:177 and smoke-test-hpc.yml both hard-fail on it), since
  a runner-local default would be invisible to compute nodes -- the classic
  wrong-work-directory bug HPC.md warns about. An unset value is what produced
  "mkdir: cannot create directory '/transfer-e2e-<run id>': Read-only file
  system"; push-tree now refuses such a path instead.

  Nothing else needs setting, contrary to what this entry used to claim:
    * vars.HPC_CI_WORK_DIR is optional. build-on-hpc:182 does
      work_dir="${WORK_DIR_INPUT:-$RUNNER_TEMP}", and nothing local has to
      survive a re-run because reattach goes through the scheduler by job name.
      Only worth setting if the runner volume runs out of disk.
    * the troika user secret is HPC_CI_SSH_USER, not TROIKA_USER. TROIKA_USER is
      only the env-var name inside the composite actions.

